    <item>
      <title>Appropriators Slash Trump’s $17B Golden Dome Request in Draft Bill</title>
      <link>https://neodymium.world/articles/appropriators-slash-trump-s-17b-golden-dome-request-in-draft-bill-091672.html</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="true">https://neodymium.world/articles/appropriators-slash-trump-s-17b-golden-dome-request-in-draft-bill-091672.html</guid>
      <pubDate>Thu, 19 Nov 2026 02:36:22 -0500</pubDate>
      <dc:creator>Amarjeet Singh</dc:creator>
      <!-- Description: executive summary or first key takeaway only (no full HTML body).
           This keeps the RSS file small and avoids duplicate-content issues with Google. -->
      <description><![CDATA[
        Senate Republicans just reality-checked the White House&#39;s ambitious missile defense timeline, slashing the $17B Golden Dome request down to roughly $9B in a new draft defense bill. Here is what this means for U.S. deterrence architecture.
        
        [SPLIT]
        ⚡ Budget experts warn that tying nearly all of the initial funding to a contentious $350 billion reconciliation package left the program dangerously vulnerable.
        [SPLIT]
        ⚡ Appropriators have demanded an independent cost estimate from CAPE within 90 days to challenge the White House&#39;s long-term financial projections.
        [SPLIT]
        🔗 Read full report → https://neodymium.world/articles/appropriators-slash-trump-s-17b-golden-dome-request-in-draft-bill-091672.html
      ]]></description>
      
